# The Docker build context is the repository root (see Dockerfile). Everything
# the API image has no use for is kept out of it: a smaller context uploads to
# the builder faster, and nothing excluded here can be baked into an image by
# accident.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.vscode
.claude
.agents
docs
infra
output
tmp
tests
README.md
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md
PROJECT_ROADMAP.md
agentskill.md

# Secrets, and beyond that a file baked in here would shadow the variables the
# platform sets — a container quietly running against someone's laptop database.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Regenerated inside the image by apps/api's postinstall hook. The host's copy
# is gitignored, so it may be stale or built on a different platform entirely.
apps/api/src/generated

# apps/web is deployed to Vercel, not from this image. Its manifest is the one
# thing needed, and only so the frozen-lockfile check sees the whole workspace.
apps/web/*
!apps/web/package.json